MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "PTXmas and That's Christmas To Me connect directly with the Christmas albums I have chosen repeatedly, so both feel like natural next listens.",
    "Their vocal harmonies also connect with my interest in The New Old Fashioned; That's Christmas To Me brings together the holiday songs and ensemble singing I want this visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Summer Horns does not satisfy my interest in vocal harmonies, even if it might share a relaxed listening mood with some holiday music.",
    "Oldies, solo pop, a country retrospective, and the Harry Potter title give me little reason to expect the holiday ensemble vocals I want. Duets alone are not enough to make that connection."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections seem to stretch my interest in Christmas albums into a broader interest in nostalgic or easygoing music, which is not enough to make me choose something.",
    "An apparent connection through singing or familiar performers seems to count too much when the songs do not clearly fit my holiday listening."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Christmas album choices suggest that holiday songs matter more to this visit than a loose similarity in mood.",
    "The combination of Christmas songs and vocal harmonies matters most; I would choose That's Christmas To Me and leave PTXmas for another visit rather than select both."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in holiday vocals but stretched it too far into music that lacks that specific appeal."
}
